odAsyncError` is defined in `packages/zod/src/v4/core/core.ts` L166.\n\n### 3. Does the rejection test assert exact class/message?\n\nNo. `transform.test.ts` L123 uses bare `.toThrow()`, so the test **does not** constrain the error class (`$ZodAsyncError` vs. anything else) or any message. The class-level identification of `$ZodAsyncError` rests on the runtime source above, which is inference from implementation — the test file itself asserts only \"throws something.\"\n\n### Separation of evidence\n\n- **Test-file facts (validated):** the three test outcomes above and their exact line spans.\n- **Implementation inference (static reading, not executed):** the `instanceof Promise` guard and `$ZodAsyncError` throw, plus the class definition at `core.ts:166`.\n- **Unresolved:** what an *arbitrary* user transform callback would do with a non-Promise return (e.g., plain value in sync mode) is not exercised here; the sync payload-mutation path after L3858 and backward (`$ZodEncodeError`) behavior (L3845–3847) are only touched in other tests not read for this question. No code or tests were executed; all conclusions are from static file reads.", "gate": {"native_rejection": false, "observed_tools": ["glob", "grep", "list", "read"], "status": "exercised", "tool_cycles": 9}, "intermediate_text": ["", "", "", "", "", "", "", "", ""], "monotonic_end": 4105814.087081208, "monotonic_start": 4105796.352325958, "operational_complete": true, "requests": [{"ambiguous_in_flight": false, "assistant": {"annotations": [], "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Find Zod v4 classic transform tests. Snapshot path—list root.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"function": {"arguments": "{\"limit\":60}", "name": "list"}, "id": "799fc127-33c4-410a-a26f-c7bd4fcb0bf4", "type": "function"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 1.3267520419321954, "ended_utc": "2026-10-08T01:46:47.089044+00:00", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "http_status": 200, "intent_utc": "2026-10-08T01:46:45.749977+00:00